return {
["17:00"]={"Next day at \003five o’clock\004 she married Tom Buchanan without so much as a shiver, and started off on a three months’ trip to the South Seas.","The Great Gatsby","F. Scott Fitzgerald"},
["17:01"]={"\003One minute after five\004. The seated guests were told that the ceremony would begin shortly. A little more patience was required.","Trouble & Triumph: A Novel of Power & Beauty","Tip “T.I.” Harris with David Ritz"},
["17:02"]={"“\003Two minutes past five\004.”\n“Then the deal is closed. And as long as I pay the remaining ninety percent within thirty days, Shifnal Farm is mine.”","Mightier Than the Sword","Jeffrey Archer"},
["17:03"]={"I looked down at the watch Trey had given me last Christmas, the delicate gold links so real and solid, and it seemed like someone else’s memory strapped to someone else’s shaking hand. It was \0035:03\004 now. I was halfway to my house.","Mother May I","Joshilyn Jackson"},
["17:04"]={"Frank Wamsley spotted his cousin Barbara and her husband and waved to them. Just ahead, he saw Marvin and his two friends. Suddenly the whole bridge convulsed. The time was \0035:04 P.M.\004 Steel screamed.","The Mothman Prophecies","John A. Keel"},
["17:05"]={"At approximately \0035:05 p.m.\004 Joe became aware of a man standing close to the table, about two metres away, talking in Mandarin into a mobile phone. He was a middle-aged Han wearing cheap leather slip-on shoes, high-waisted black trousers and a white short-sleeved shirt.","Typhoon","Charles Cumming"},
["17:06"]={"The rain stopped \003around 5 p.m.\004 and a few of those people who were out and about expressed mild surprise when the rainbow failed to fade.","Mortality (The Rainbow)","Nicholas Royle"},
["17:07"]={"As I looked at its huge dial, and at the pendulum moving to and fro regularly and slowly in Space, as if its swinging meant to divide eternity, I saw its needles pointing to \003seven minutes past five\004.","Nightmare Tales","H.P. Blavatsky"},
["17:08"]={"The last communication we had with Dwight Sloane was yesterday. \003Five-oh-eight P.M.\004 Here. He put his finger on a lake called Embarrass. “He should have checked in four hours later. He didn’t.”","Boundary Waters","William Kent Krueger"},
["17:09"]={"She looked at her watch and saw it was \003nine minutes past five\004. “It’s happening, Daddy! The sun’s going out!”\n“Yes,” he agreed.","Gerald’s Game","Stephen King"},
["17:10"]={"Didna ye hear the pipes, my leddy? he rejoined.\n“Yes, well enough; but a whole regiment of pipes can’t make it six o’clock when my watch says \003ten minutes past five\004.”","Malcom","George MacDonald"},
["17:11"]={"At \003eleven minutes past five\004 Dick Bellamy stopped Melchard’s car outside the booking-office of somnolent Harthborough’s dead-alive station — the junction of the single-line track to Whitebay and its bathing machines with the double-track branch of the G.N.R.","Ambrotox and Limping Dick","Oliver Fleming"},
["17:12"]={"“Well, here we are,” said Colonel Julyan, “and it’s exactly \003twelve minutes past five\004. We shall catch them in the middle of their tea. Better wait for a bit.”\nMaxim lit a cigarette, and then stretched out his hand to me. He did not speak.","Rebecca","Daphne du Maurier"},
["17:13"]={"So at \00317:13\004 Callum Green was buying a necklace and something like a couple hours later he was dead.","Lie in Wait","G.J Minett"},
["17:14"]={"Do you know what time it is, Atticus? she said. “Exactly \003fourteen minutes past five\004. The alarm clock’s set for five-thirty. I want you to know that.”","To Kill a Mockingbird","Harper Lee"},
["17:15"]={"It was only a \003quarter past five\004, but the evening was as dark as midnight. And when he reached the edge of the porch the rain began falling.","A Taste for Death","P.D. James"},
["17:16"]={"I think the first one I remember happening was on the London Underground, Circle line, \00317:16 p.m.\004\nShe went on to describe what had happened or not quite happened.","Money Never Sleeps","Stella Whitelaw"},
["17:17"]={"And it was just \003seventeen minutes past five\004 when Dick French, hanging in a frenzy of anxiety over the paddock fence circling the inside of the mile oval, uttered something resembling a howl and rushed to the gate to signal his recreant driver.","The Flying Mercury","Eleanor M. Ingram"},
["17:18"]={"Lupin rose, without breaking his contemptuous silence, and took the sheet of paper. I remembered soon after that, at this moment, I happened to look at the clock. It was \003eighteen minutes past five\004.","The Confessions of Arsène Lupin","Maurice LeBlanc"},
["17:19"]={"Scott eased himself into the corner before once again checking the little sulphur dots on his watch. It was \0035:19\004. He and Hannah had been in the safe for an hour and seventeen minutes.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["17:20"]={"I’m going to park here and walk in. I don’t want to drive into a zoo. He glanced at his watch. “It’s only \003five-twenty\004. Kidnapper’s call is supposed to come at six. We’ve got time.”","Purgatory Ridge","William Kent Krueger"},
["17:22"]={"I expect she didn’t want Octavia to know that she’d called in her father, not until they’d worked out a plan. And I was the one who fixed the time. I didn’t see how I could catch a train before the \003seventeen-twenty-two\004 which gets in to Waterloo at nineteen-twenty-nine.","A Certain Justice","P.D. James"},
["17:23"]={"I was wondering if we could meet for a drink.\n“What for?”\n“Just for a chat. Do you know the Royal batsman, near Central Station? We could meet tomorrow at five?”\n“\003Five twenty-three\004,” I said, to exert some control over the situation.","A Fraction of the Whole","Steve Toltz"},
["17:25"]={"Now, said Handsley, when Angela had poured out the last cup, “it’s \003twenty-five minutes past five\004, at half-past the Murder game is on.”","A Man Lay Dead","Ngaio Marsh"},
["17:26"]={"There’s a train that leaves Totnes at \003twenty-six minutes past five\004 this afternoon, I said, “and it reaches London at—”","Wildtrack","Bernard Cornwell"},
["17:27"]={"One evening at \0035:27\004, when Septimus was closing the file on the last claim for the day, his immediate superior, the deputy manager, called him in for a consultation.","Broken Routine","Jeffrey Archer"},
["17:28"]={"And so, when he told her on May 15 at \0035:28\004 in the afternoon that he had to be moving on, she passed out. She was in his bed at the time.","Smart Women","Judy Blume"},
["17:29"]={"Well? he said.\n“It’s \003twenty-nine minutes past five\004, Insert Name Here,” said the imp nervously.","Thud!","Terry Pratchett"},
["17:30"]={"It was \003half-past five\004 before Holmes returned. He was bright, eager, and in excellent spirits, a mood which in his case alternated with fits of the blackest depression.","The Sign of Four","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle"},
["17:31"]={"They discussed the transmission: which of their friends, they wondered, was responsible for it? But at \00317:31\004 Pick called back","Heavy Water","Martin Amis"},
["17:32"]={"It was exactly \003thirty-two minutes past five o’clock\004 on the evening of Friday, December 9th, when the station-master at Anerly received the following communication by wire from the signal box at Froest Hill: 5:28 down from London Bridge just passed.","Cleek, the Master Detective","Thomas W. Hanshew"},
["17:33"]={"He and Lady Ursula were back at number sixty-two by \003five thirty-three\004. He could remember the time exactly because he had looked at the car clock.","A Taste for Death","P.D. James"},
["17:35"]={"At \0035:35\004, he got word over the radio that Helmunth Hanover of the Aurora Sentinel had received a call from an anonymous spokesperson for the Minnesota Civilian Brigade threatening some form of retaliation if the Indians fished.","Iron Lake","William Kent Krueger"},
["17:37"]={"Look, Lucille, said Joe when Lucille strolled into the office at \0035:37\004. “I don’t know what you said to this gal, but it seems to have had exactly the opposite of the desired effect. She’s got some bee in her bonnet about Harvard Law School.”","Lightning Rods","Helen DeWitt"},
["17:38"]={"He stares at the phone, thinks: Ring. Ring now. But it remains inert. \0035:38 p.m.\004 Bunny will be done with her housekeeping shift by now.","Cloud Cuckoo Land","Anthony Doerr"},
["17:39"]={"It’s \00305:39\004 so we can have dinner, it’s quick noodles. While they’re in the hot water, Ma finds hard words to test me from the milk carton like nutritional that means food, and pasteurized that means laser guns zapped away the germs.","Room","Emma Donoghue"},
["17:40"]={"As no one had “any other business” to raise, I closed the meeting at \0035:40\004, and suggested to Jeremy that he join Rosemary and me for dinner. I wanted to see them together.","Trial and Error","Jeffrey Archer"},
["17:43"]={"“I always prefer to travel on a British carrier,” Don Pedro told the purser as they were shown to their seats in first class. The Boeing Stratocruiser took off at \0035:43 p.m.\004, just a few minutes behind schedule.","Best Kept Secret","Jeffrey Archer"},
["17:44"]={"Janice is not waiting for him in the lounge or beside the pool when at last \003around 5:45\004 they come home from playing the par-5 eighteenth. Instead one of the girls in their green and white uniforms comes over and tells him that his wife wants him to call home.","Rabbit Is Rich","John Updike"},
["17:45"]={"“A \003quarter to six\004,” answered the midwife.\n“And what if I really am dying?” thought Olga Mihalovna, looking at her husband’s head and the window-panes on which the rain was beating.","The Party","Anton Pavlovich Chekhov"},
["17:46"]={"At \003fourteen minutes to six\004 they walked into the director’s study, where a young lady of Sally’s age offered the guests a choice of dry sherry or orange juice.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["17:48"]={"Father came home at \0035:48 p.m.\004 I heard him come through the front door. Then he came into the living room. He was wearing a lime green and sky blue check shirt and there was a double knot on one of his shoes but not on the other.","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["17:49"]={"\0035:49 P.M.\004, SUNDAY, JUNE 8TH, 1924 WHEN ODELL ARRIVED back at Camp IV, he was unable to conceal his excitement. He crawled into Norton’s tent and told him what he’d seen.","Paths of Glory","Jeffrey Archer"},
["17:50"]={"Esterville had called the truck stop, but no one had seen his wife come in. She hadn’t returned home. Cork and McDougal found her red Mustang at \0035:50\004.","Corpus Delicti","William Kent Krueger"},
["17:51"]={"The sun was red and the shadows were long and dark. It wanted but \003nine minutes to six\004, and within the hotel the disgraceful National Swill was in full flow, men pouring as much liquor down their throats as possible before the fatal hour of drought arrived.","Venom House","Arthur Upfield"},
["17:52"]={"It was \003eight minutes to six o’clock\004. “I must get him,” he told the telephone girl for the dozenth time.\n“Sorry— no one will answer,” she said wearily.","Jimmy Kirkland and the Plot for a Pennant","Hugh S. Fullerton"},
["17:53"]={"That boy will be spoiled, as sure as I go on springs; he’s made such a lot of. Have you been regulated?\n“I should think I have!” exclaimed I, in indignant recollection of my education.\n“All right; keep your temper. What time are you?”\n“\003Seven minutes to six\004.”","The Adventures of a Three-Guinea Watch","Talbot Baines Reed"},
["17:54"]={"It was \0035:54 p.m.\004 when Father came back into the living room. He said, “What is this?” but he said it very quietly and I didn’t realise that he was angry because he wasn’t shouting.","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["17:55"]={"The wind moaned and sang dismally, catching the ears and lifting the shabby coat-tails of Mr. Mortimer Jenkyn, ‘Photographic Artist’, as he stood outside and put the shutters up with this own cold hands in despair of further trade. It was \003five minutes to six\004.","The Deferred Appointment","Algernon Blackwood"},
["17:56"]={"Now, sir, the hand wants \003four minutes to six\004. If the hour strike before you call yourself a wanton, gratuitous calumniator, I’ll flog you round the room.","The Knight of Gwynne","Charles James Lever"},
["17:57"]={"At \003three minutes to six\004, despite there still being no sign of Sally, the director suggested they should all make their way to the Great Hall.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["17:58"]={"Then I notice the windows: they’re shiny dark. \00317:58\004, insists my watch. It can’t be. It’s only just gone four. I peer around my tormentor’s belly to find Immaculée Constantin, but she’s gone.","The Bone Clocks","David Mitchell"},
["17:59"]={"When he arrived it was \003nearly six o’clock\004, and the sun was setting full and warm, and the red light streamed in through the window and gave more colour to the pale cheeks.","Dracula","Bram Stoker"},
}
